<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kamboja</h1><p class="st-meta">700 BCE – 330 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A warlike people of the Hindu Kush borderlands, counted among the sixteen mahajanapadas and famous across ancient India for their horses.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Kambojas are named by the grammarian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panini">Panini</a> and in Buddhist lists of the sixteen great states. They lived north-west of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-gandhara">Gandhara</a>, probably in north-eastern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/islamic-emirate-of-afghanistan-2021-present">Afghanistan</a> and the hills of north-western <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/islamic-republic-of-pakistan">Pakistan</a>. The Vedic etymologist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaska">Yaska</a> noted that they used an Iranian word for to go, and many scholars see them as an Iranian-speaking people.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chanakya">Kautilya's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arthashastra">Arthashastra</a> describes the Kambojas as a sangha whose members lived by trade and arms, suggesting rule by a warrior aristocracy rather than a king. Indian literature praised Kamboja horses and cavalry, and the epics place Kamboja horsemen on the battlefield. Little else is known of their society or religion.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Their lands fell under Achaemenid rule and were overrun by Alexander's army around 327 BCE; some scholars identify the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aspasioi">Aspasioi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assakenoi">Assakenoi</a> he fought as Kamboja groups. The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/maurya-empire">Maurya Empire</a> later absorbed them, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashoka">Ashoka's</a> edicts name the Kambojas among the frontier peoples of his realm.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 700 BCE – 330 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">South Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:45.77%;width:7.36%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>700 BCE – 330 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Iranian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, <a href="/countries/pakistan">Pakistan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kamboja Mahajanapada, Kambojas</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-515&amp;focus=kamboja" aria-label="Kamboja on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6374 932 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kamboja lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6140 1251h0M5548 987h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6694 1188h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M6694 1188h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Afghanistan. <a href="/atlas?year=-515&amp;focus=kamboja">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

